> One minor annoyance to this plan will be the energy
> drain caused by the Amulet.  So my question is this: Once I reach the
> Astral Plane, can I safely drop the Amulet? 

You can always drop the Amulet. Rodney, for example, will steal it whether
it's on the floor or in your inventory; there's no difference in practise.
But why leave it in a corner, as you say below?

> I was thinking I could
> drop the Amulet in a corner somewhere, go off and kill all the hordes,

In an extinctionist game the hordes are, actually, only 30 (or so) humans
(mainly priests), and the riders. Once you've killed the humans you have
to handle the resurrecting riders, only. Yes, you can drop the Amulet.

> and pick it up when I'm done.  If the Amulet has been #named (so I can
> identify it later), is there any reason for me not to do this?

I am unsure whether the Amulet could be disintegrated (along with the
covetous monster that picked it up) by a black dragon (in case those are
still non-extinct at that time). No issue anyway if you've extincted all
those black dragons.

> Thanks for any comments or thoughts!

If you're picky to do a 100% extinction mind that you may miss some of
the monsters, especially those that are non-detectable by telepathy;
search thoroughly in that case. Another point is that you need to create
monsters on various dungeon depths so that all possible monsters will be
created. And in case you're not playing a wizard it might become a very
boring procedure to extinct everything (been there, done that, never do
that again).

